IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part I, "Disentitlement to Benefits" and "Deductions from Benefits": ss 18, 19, 20.
-- Layer 1 of piece ei1. Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
-- A percentage or fraction of earnings or benefits is rounded to the nearest dollar by the core's
-- `s 6(2) and s 152.01(5) amount rounded to the nearest dollar`, cited here as s 6(2).

§ `Section 18 - availability for work`

-- src:449 | 18 (1) A claimant is not entitled to be paid benefits for a working day in a benefit period for which the claimant fails to prove that on that day the claimant was
-- src:450 | (a) capable of and available for work and unable to obtain suitable employment;
-- Paragraph (a) has three limbs, all of which the claimant must prove. "Suitable employment" is for s 6(4) (the
-- fact "unable to obtain suitable employment" is an input here).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 18(1)(a) (src:449-450)
GIVEN `the claimant was capable of work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant was available for work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant was unable to obtain suitable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(1)(a) the claimant was capable of and available for work and unable to obtain suitable employment` IF
        `the claimant was capable of work`
    AND `the claimant was available for work`
    AND `the claimant was unable to obtain suitable employment`

-- src:451 | (b) unable to work because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine, and that the claimant would otherwise be available for work; or
-- src:452 | (c) engaged in jury service.
-- src:453 | Exception
-- src:454 | (2) A claimant to whom benefits are payable under any of sections 23 to 23.3 is not disentitled under paragraph (1)(b) for failing to prove that he or she would have been available for work were it not for the illness, injury or quarantine.
-- "Prescribed illness, injury or quarantine" is the Regulations' (reg 40, piece er3). A claimant to whom benefits are
-- payable under any of sections 23 to 23.3 does not have to prove that they would otherwise be available (subsection (2)).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 18(1)(b), s 18(2) (src:451) (src:454)
GIVEN `the claimant was unable to work because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant would otherwise have been available for work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `benefits are payable to the claimant under any of sections 23 to 23.3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(1)(b) and s 18(2) the claimant was unable to work because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` IF
        `the claimant was unable to work because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine`
    AND (`the claimant would otherwise have been available for work` OR `benefits are payable to the claimant under any of sections 23 to 23.3`)

-- src:452 | (c) engaged in jury service.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 18(1)(c) (src:452)
GIVEN `the claimant was engaged in jury service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(1)(c) the claimant was engaged in jury service` IF
    `the claimant was engaged in jury service`

-- src:449 | 18 (1) A claimant is not entitled to be paid benefits for a working day in a benefit period for which the claimant fails to prove that on that day the claimant was
-- The rule bites on "a working day" (any day but Saturday and Sunday: reg 32, piece er2). On a working day the claimant
-- is entitled, as far as this section goes, only if they prove one of the three things.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 18(1) (src:449)
GIVEN -- out of range: reg 32 (piece er2)
      `the day is a working day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant proves that on that day paragraph (a) was met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant proves that on that day paragraph (b) was met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant proves that on that day paragraph (c) was met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(1) the claimant is entitled to be paid benefits for the day as far as section 18 goes` IF
        NOT (`the day is a working day`)
     OR `the claimant proves that on that day paragraph (a) was met`
     OR `the claimant proves that on that day paragraph (b) was met`
     OR `the claimant proves that on that day paragraph (c) was met`

§ `Section 19 - deductions for earnings`

-- src:458 | 19 (1) If a claimant has earnings during their waiting period, an amount not exceeding those earnings shall, as prescribed, be deducted from the benefits payable for the first three weeks for which benefits are otherwise payable.
-- The amount "as prescribed" is the Regulations' (reg 39, piece er3: the earnings themselves, up to the claimant's
-- weekly rate of benefits); it is an input. The deduction does not exceed the earnings.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 19(1) (src:458)
GIVEN `the claimant's earnings during their waiting period` IS A NUMBER
      -- out of range: reg 39 (piece er3)
      `the amount that the regulations prescribe be deducted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 19(1) the amount deducted from the benefits payable for the first three weeks for which benefits are otherwise payable` IS
    min `the claimant's earnings during their waiting period` `the amount that the regulations prescribe be deducted`

-- src:460 | (2) Subject to subsections (3), (4), 21(3) and 22(5), if the claimant has earnings during any other week of unemployment, there shall be deducted from benefits payable in that week the amount equal to the total of
-- src:461 | (a) 50% of the earnings that are less than or equivalent to 90% of the claimant’s weekly insurable earnings, and
-- src:462 | (b) 100% of the earnings that are greater than 90% of the claimant’s weekly insurable earnings.
-- (a) 50% of the earnings up to 90% of the claimant's weekly insurable earnings; (b) 100% of the earnings above that.
-- Each amount that is a percentage of earnings is rounded under s 6(2): the 90% line, and each of the two deductions
-- (fork F-round in NOTES.md).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 19(2), s 6(2) (src:460-462)
GIVEN `the claimant's earnings in the week of unemployment` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant's weekly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 19(2) the amount deducted from the benefits payable in the week` IS
    `s 6(2) and s 152.01(5) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` (50% TIMES min `the claimant's earnings in the week of unemployment` `90% of the claimant's weekly insurable earnings`)
    PLUS `s 6(2) and s 152.01(5) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` (max 0 (`the claimant's earnings in the week of unemployment` MINUS `90% of the claimant's weekly insurable earnings`))
    WHERE
        `90% of the claimant's weekly insurable earnings` MEANS
            `s 6(2) and s 152.01(5) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` (90% TIMES `the claimant's weekly insurable earnings`)

-- A deduction is taken "from benefits payable in that week", so it cannot take them below nothing (assumed, not
-- ruled: fork F-floor in NOTES.md).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 19(2) (src:460)
GIVEN `the benefits payable in the week before the deduction` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount deducted from the benefits payable in the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 19(2) the benefits payable in the week after the deduction` IS
    max 0 (`the benefits payable in the week before the deduction` MINUS `the amount deducted from the benefits payable in the week`)

-- src:464 | (3) If the claimant has failed to declare all or some of their earnings to the Commission for a period, determined under the regulations, for which benefits were claimed,
-- src:465 | (a) the following amount shall be deducted from the benefits paid to the claimant for that period:
-- src:466 | (i) the amount of the undeclared earnings, if, in the opinion of the Commission, the claimant knowingly failed to declare the earnings, or
-- src:467 | (ii) in any other case, the amount of the undeclared earnings less the difference between
-- src:468 | (A) all amounts determined under paragraph (2)(a) or (b) for the period,
-- src:469 | and
-- src:470 | (B) all amounts that were applied under those paragraphs in respect of the declared earnings for the period; and
-- The Commission's opinion that the claimant "knowingly" failed to declare is an input. (A) is the total of the s 19(2)
-- amounts for the period (counting all earnings); (B) the part of it applied to the declared earnings.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 19(3)(a) (src:464-470)
GIVEN `in the opinion of the Commission, the claimant knowingly failed to declare the earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the undeclared earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `all amounts determined under paragraph (2)(a) or (b) for the period` IS A NUMBER
      `all amounts that were applied under those paragraphs in respect of the declared earnings for the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 19(3)(a) the amount deducted from the benefits paid to the claimant for the period` IS
    IF `in the opinion of the Commission, the claimant knowingly failed to declare the earnings`
    THEN `the amount of the undeclared earnings`
    ELSE `the amount of the undeclared earnings` MINUS (`all amounts determined under paragraph (2)(a) or (b) for the period` MINUS `all amounts that were applied under those paragraphs in respect of the declared earnings for the period`)

-- src:471 | (b) the deduction shall be made
-- src:472 | (i) from the benefits paid for a number of weeks that begins with the first week for which the earnings were not declared in that period, and
-- src:473 | (ii) in such a manner that the amount deducted in each consecutive week equals the claimant’s benefits paid for that week.
-- The deduction starts with the first week for which the earnings were not declared and takes, in each consecutive
-- week, the whole of the benefits paid for that week, until the amount is used up (the last week takes what is left).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 19(3)(b) (src:471-473)
GIVEN `the amount still to be deducted` IS A NUMBER
      `the benefits paid for each consecutive week, starting with the first week for which the earnings were not declared` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `s 19(3)(b) the amount deducted in each consecutive week` IS
    CONSIDER `the benefits paid for each consecutive week, starting with the first week for which the earnings were not declared`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN paid FOLLOWED BY later THEN
        IF `the amount still to be deducted` AT MOST 0
        THEN EMPTY
        ELSE (min `the amount still to be deducted` paid) FOLLOWED BY `s 19(3)(b) the amount deducted in each consecutive week` (`the amount still to be deducted` MINUS min `the amount still to be deducted` paid) later

-- src:475 | (4) Earnings from employment under an employment support measure other than one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d) and earnings or allowances payable to a claimant for attending a course or program of instruction or training shall not be deducted under this section except in accordance with the regulations.
-- Earnings from employment under an employment support measure other than one in paragraph 59(c) or (d), and earnings
-- or allowances for attending a course or program, are deducted only as the regulations provide. The deposited
-- Regulations cite subsection 19(4) only once, in a transitional section (piece er6), and name no general rule, so
-- whether the regulations provide for the deduction is an input.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 19(4) (src:475)
GIVEN `the earnings are from employment under an employment support measure` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 59 (piece ei2)
      `that measure is one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earnings or allowances are payable to the claimant for attending a course or program of instruction or training` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations provide for the earnings or allowances to be deducted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 19(4) the earnings or allowances may be deducted under section 19` IF
        NOT (   (`the earnings are from employment under an employment support measure` AND NOT (`that measure is one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d)`))
             OR `the earnings or allowances are payable to the claimant for attending a course or program of instruction or training`)
     OR `the regulations provide for the earnings or allowances to be deducted`

§ `Section 20 - deductions for days on which the claimant is not entitled`

-- src:477 | 20 (1) If a claimant is not entitled to receive benefits for a working day in their waiting period, an amount equal to 1/5 of their weekly rate of benefits for each such working day shall be deducted from the benefits payable for the three weeks described in subsection 19(1).
-- 1/5 of the weekly rate of benefits for each such working day, rounded to the nearest dollar under s 6(2) for each day
-- (fork F-day in NOTES.md), taken from the benefits payable for the three weeks of s 19(1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 20(1), s 6(2) (src:477)
GIVEN `the claimant's weekly rate of benefits` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of working days in the waiting period for which the claimant is not entitled to receive benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 20(1) the amount deducted for the excluded days in the waiting period` IS
    `s 6(2) and s 152.01(5) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` (`the claimant's weekly rate of benefits` DIVIDED BY 5)
    TIMES `the number of working days in the waiting period for which the claimant is not entitled to receive benefits`

-- src:479 | (2) If a claimant is disentitled from receiving benefits for a working day in a week of unemployment that is not in their waiting period, an amount equal to 1/5 of their weekly rate of benefits for each such working day shall be deducted from the benefits payable for that week.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 20(2), s 6(2) (src:479)
GIVEN `the claimant's weekly rate of benefits` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of working days in the week of unemployment, not in the waiting period, for which the claimant is disentitled from receiving benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 20(2) the amount deducted for the days of disentitlement in a week that is not in the waiting period` IS
    `s 6(2) and s 152.01(5) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` (`the claimant's weekly rate of benefits` DIVIDED BY 5)
    TIMES `the number of working days in the week of unemployment, not in the waiting period, for which the claimant is disentitled from receiving benefits`
